    "title": "Home Team Friday Week 12 MVP - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ronald Clark ,\n16 minutes ago\nLINCOLN CITY, Ind. (WEHT) — After counting up 7,469 total votes, Heritage Hills’ Dalton Pledger was named our Week 12 Home Team Friday MVP of the night.\nThe senior running back rushed for 112 yards on 19 carries for two touchdowns, while also adding six tackles on defense. Pledger was wreaking havoc on both sides of the ball for the Patriots in their 38-8 win over Jasper in the 4A sectional championship. He secured 74 percent of the votes to claim MVP.\n“The only way that I’ve been able to pull this off all year is my o-line,” he said. “They’re all great. They move defenses for me and they just create opportunities. So that’s kind of awesome.”\nPledger and Heritage Hills will host Martinsville on Friday, November 14th in the 4A regional championship.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
